            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TwinMommy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Been looking for a gooey coconut cookie for a while and this is the one. Substituted dried cranberries for the raisins and added much less cinnamon(1/2 tsp). They turned out great!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amanda Dunsmore"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really enjoyed these cookies - fast and easy to make with I had around the kitchen! I'm not a huge fan of cinnamon and raisins with coconut, so I left the raisins out and substituted 2 tbsp cocoa powder for the cinnamon, and about an extra 1/4 cup coconut to make up for the missing raisins. Fantastic! Was worried at first it wasn't moist enough as the mixture wouldn't hold together after stirring, but I found it held together fine when I hand formed the dough into egg sized shapes and flattened them a bit. Cooked them for about 10 min too, since I made 16 slightly larger cookies instead 18. So glad I made these soft, chewy scrumptious cookies!",
            "datePublished": "2013-01-03T21:01:20.293Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jjlee2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These cookies were awesome! I had to add about 1/4 cup of water to the batter to make it more dough-like. I added chocolate chips instead of raisins and they came out AWESOME. Huge hit with all my friends! They were chewy and moist! The recipe calls for \"egg sized\" heaps of dough, so they are MASSIVE cookies. I liked that about the cookies, but obviously some people might want to ration out the dough a little more with smaller sized dollops of dough. Not over-powering coconut taste which I liked too!",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-26T17:29:33.760Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lauren"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great cookies! I substituted chocolate chips for the raisins and didn't put any glaze on them. I definately recommend these! They did take about 15 minutes to cook instead of 8, but they are wonderful; sightly crispy edges with a soft chewy inside. Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2006-06-09T21:35:21.733Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Valerie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made these with half the amount of sugar that was called for and added some apple sauce to add the sweetness and a little moisture back into the dough. \nI also chopped up some dried apricots and prunes that I had on hand instead of the rasins and it came out excellent. The cookie was not overly sweet and the dried fruit added a little more to each bite.",
            "datePublished": "2006-12-21T08:52:10.180Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
